  "id": "COMPOUND:27179 - PROTEIN:5999",
  "verbalization": "Beta-Fenchyl alcohol appears to interact with multiple targets that ultimately lead to the activation of Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein. The evidence suggests that beta-Fenchyl alcohol acts as a target for compounds such as Npc151898 and Pterocarpol, which in turn target the Sodium/bile acid cotransporter. This chain of interactions implies a potential role for beta-Fenchyl alcohol in modulating signaling pathways involving bile acid transport and subsequent cellular responses. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the same downstream effect—Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein—suggests a broader functional role for beta-Fenchyl alcohol in macrophage activation or response. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of beta-Fenchyl alcohol in influencing macrophage-related processes through indirect mechanisms involving bile acid transport and receptor activation.",
